{"id": "EUVD-2026-107886", "enisaUuid": "80cc9d93-75df-3a11-8ff6-f7eddbdfe134", "description": "Roundcube Webmail before 1.6.20 and 1.7.x before 1.7.5 allows the disabled_actions configuration setting to be bypassed. The check compared only the action name as requested, so a remote authenticated attacker could reach an action listed in disabled_actions by requesting it through its deprecated alias instead. Upstream fixed this in the commit \u201cFix bug where deprecated action aliases bypassed `disabled_actions` setting\u201d, which moves the check into rcmail::action_handler() and resolves aliases before comparing.", "datePublished": "2026-10-22T01:36:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-22T01:36:10", "baseScore": 3.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:N/I:L/A:N", "references": ["https://bugs.debian.org/1151279", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/commit/cd413140bf5362cd86a4327dd6364387505865a9", "https://roundcube.net/news/2026/10/19/security-updates-1.6.20-and-1.7.5", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/releases/tag/1.7.5", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/releases/tag/1.6.20", "https://github.com/roundcube/roundcubemail/commit/e7c512ae09ebd0ae5d0d2f29e00a767bf91f6bbe"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-114721", "GHSA-8f65-rc5r-w7c8"], "assigner": "mitre", "epss": 0.3, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "79d2f499-37c2-3691-b171-a6fe7f9aa95d", "product": {"name": "Webmail", "vendor": {"name": "bulwarkmail"}}, "product_version": "1.7.0 <1.7.5"}, {"id": "87b68451-f488-3dc4-ab4d-90bc3ab58966", "product": {"name": "Webmail", "vendor": {"name": "bulwarkmail"}}, "product_version": "1.6.0 <1.6.20"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "3ac89384-3a3d-3fcb-8ea9-399c9f424784", "vendor": {"name": "Roundcube"}}], "isExploited": false}